  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Slalom and shoot",
  "description": "The players stand in a line, each with a ball. The first dribbles straight ahead to a slalom of cones, dribbles through the cones and, after the last one, makes a quick change of direction before shooting at goal. Fetch your ball and join the back of the line.\n\nWith two goals you can run two courses side by side. Let someone try being goalkeeper. Works well for young children, from about 7 years old. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Small touches close to your feet in the slalom."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Use both the inside and the outside of your foot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Look up at the goal before you shoot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Make the turn quick – that is what gets you free."
    }
  ],
